Create /storage/.gitignore with this complete content. It preserves the runtime directory structure and .gitkeep placeholders while ignoring runtime files by default.

MedOrbits -- Runtime Storage Security

Ignore all runtime files by default.

Preserve Git ignore rules and directory placeholders.

!.gitignore
!.gitkeep
!README.md

Preserve runtime directory structure.

!uploads/
!documents/
!applications/
!profiles/
!employer-documents/
!generated/
!exports/
!quarantine/
!backups/

Ignore all runtime contents.

uploads/*
documents/*
applications/*
profiles/*
employer-documents/*
generated/*
exports/*
quarantine/*
backups/*

Preserve directory placeholders.

!uploads/.gitkeep
!documents/.gitkeep
!applications/.gitkeep
!profiles/.gitkeep
!employer-documents/.gitkeep
!generated/.gitkeep
!exports/.gitkeep
!quarantine/.gitkeep
!backups/.gitkeep

Security checks

* Save this file at exactly /storage/.gitignore.
* Ensure each listed directory contains its own .gitkeep if you want Git to preserve that empty directory.
* Git ignore rules do not remove files already tracked by Git. Check with git ls-files storage/; if sensitive files are tracked, remove them from the index carefully and rotate any exposed secrets.
* Keep uploaded documents, backups, and quarantined files outside the public web root, with server-side access controls and appropriate file permissions.